{"name":"Dusky Cyclamen","hex":"#7d6d70","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"dusky","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Dimly lit, as at dusk (evening).","Having a shade of color that is rather dark."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A dusky shark.","A dusky dolphin."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dusky"},{"term":"cyclamen","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various primulaceous flowering plants, of the genus Cyclamen, widely cultivated as a houseplant, having decorative leaves and solitary flowers.","A purplish-red colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/cyclamen"}],"entries":[{"title":"Dusky","blocks":[{"text":"Dusky is an English electronic music duo from London consisting of Alfie Granger-Howell and Nick Harriman. Formed in 2011, they have released music on various records labels, before setting up their own label 17 Steps in July 2014 with the release of the Love Taking Over EP."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dusky"},{"title":"Cyclamen","blocks":[{"text":"Cyclamen is a genus of 25 species of perennial flowering plants in the family Primulaceae. In English, it is known by the common name sowbread, or, by the genus name as cyclamen. The species are native to Europe and the Mediterranean Basin east to the Caucasus and Iran, with one species in Somalia. They grow from tubers and are valued for their flowers with upswept petals and variably patterned leaves."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/31/Cyclamen_purpurascens_sl3.jpg/330px-Cyclamen_purpurascens_sl3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyclamen"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/RakefetMetzuya.jpg/500px-RakefetMetzuya.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cd/RakefetMet